                "senderName": "NWS Twin Cities/Chanhassen MN",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 19 at 1:07AM CDT until September 19 at 5:00AM CDT by NWS Twin Cities/Chanhassen MN",
                "description": "FFWMPX\n\nThe National Weather Service in the Twin Cities has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNortheastern Faribault County in south central Minnesota...\nNorthern Freeborn County in south central Minnesota...\nSouthern Steele County in south central Minnesota...\nSouthern Waseca County in south central Minnesota...\n\n* Until 500 AM CDT.\n\n* At 107 AM CDT, local law enforcement reported thunderstorms\nproducing heavy rain in southern Waseca county along the MN Highway\n30 corridor. Between 5 and 9 inches of rain have fallen. Additional\nrainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the warned area.\nFlash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nBlooming Prairie, New Richland, Ellendale, Geneva, Hartland, Otisco\nand Matawan.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
